second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is the population of Sandusky Township, Ohio?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 131, \"text\": \"Sandusky Township, Crawford County, Ohio Sandusky Township is one of the sixteen townships of Crawford County, Ohio, United States.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d00\", \"start\": 132, \"end\": 177, \"text\": \"As of the 2010 census the population was 459.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d00\", \"start\": 178, \"end\": 308, \"text\": \"Located in the eastern part of the county, it borders the following townships: No municipalities are located in Sandusky Township.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d00\", \"start\": 309, \"end\": 400, \"text\": \"Sandusky Township was named from the Sandusky River, which flows through its southern part.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d00\", \"start\": 401, \"end\": 483, \"text\": \"Statewide, other Sandusky Townships are located in Richland and Sandusky counties.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d00\", \"start\": 484, \"end\": 650, \"text\": \"The township is governed by a three-member board of trustees, who are elected in November of odd-numbered years to a four-year term beginning on the following January\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 538, \"text\": \"from Wikimedia project Spanish Wikipedia located in the administrative territorial entity Crawford County 1 reference imported from Wikimedia project English Wikipedia coordinate location 40°51'5 '' N, 82°49'22 '' W 1 reference imported from Wikimedia project English Wikipedia population 1,234 statement is subject of 2020 United States Census determination method or standard census point in time 1 April 2020 1 reference stated in 2020 United States Census retrieved 1 January 2022 reference URL https : //data.census.gov/cedsci/table?\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d01\", \"start\": 539, \"end\": 672, \"text\": \"t=Populations % 20and % 20People & g=0100000US, % 241600000 & y=2020 editor United States Census Bureau 1,234 determination method or\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 131, \"text\": \"Sandusky Township, Crawford County, Ohio Sandusky Township is one of the sixteen townships of Crawford County, Ohio, United States.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d02\", \"start\": 132, \"end\": 179, \"text\": \"As of the 2010 census the population was 1,234.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d02\", \"start\": 180, \"end\": 310, \"text\": \"Located in the eastern part of the county, it borders the following townships: No municipalities are located in Sandusky Township.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d02\", \"start\": 311, \"end\": 402, \"text\": \"Sandusky Township was named from the Sandusky River, which flows through its southern part.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d02\", \"start\": 403, \"end\": 485, \"text\": \"Statewide, other Sandusky Townships are located in Richland and Sandusky counties.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d02\", \"start\": 486, \"end\": 653, \"text\": \"The township is governed by a three-member board of trustees, who are elected in November of odd-numbered years to a four-year term beginning on the following January.\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 63, \"text\": \"County , OH have `` super commutes '' in excess of 90 minutes .\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d03\", \"start\": 64, \"end\": 204, \"text\": \"The chart below shows how the median household income in Sandusky County , OH compares to that of it 's neighboring and parent geographies .\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d03\", \"start\": 205, \"end\": 518, \"text\": \"View Data Save Image Share / Embed Add Data to Cart View Data Save Image Share / Embed Add Data to Cart Car Ownership 2 cars Average Number The following chart displays the households in Sandusky County , OH distributed between a series of car ownership buckets compared to the national averages for each bucket .\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d03\", \"start\": 519, \"end\": 550, \"text\": \"The largest share of households\"}, \"D5S1\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d04\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 56, \"text\": \"41,228 and the median income for a family was $ 49,647 .\"}, \"D5S2\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d04\", \"start\": 57, \"end\": 124, \"text\": \"Males had a median income of $ 40,304 versus $ 28,118 for females .\"}, \"D5S3\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d04\", \"start\": 125, \"end\": 176, \"text\": \"The per capita income for the county was $ 20,590 .\"}, \"D5S4\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab:d04\", \"start\": 177, \"end\": 335, \"text\": \"About 10.8 % of families and 13.0 % of the population were below the poverty line , including 21.3 % of those under age 18 and 6.2 % of those age 65 or over .\"}, \"D5S5\":